/**
 * Monthly building approvals data (ABS Cat. 8731.0)
 * Auto-generated by scripts/refresh-data.mjs — do not edit manually.
 * Last refreshed: 2026-06-15
 *
 * ── Data source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Australian Bureau of Statistics — Building Approvals, Australia (Cat. 8731.0)
 * Table 8731009: Total dwellings approved, all sectors, by state and Australia.
 * Released monthly (~12th–15th of the following month).
 * https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/industry/building-and-construction/building-approvals-australia
 *
 * ── Methodology ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Annual run rate  = trailing 12-month sum of total dwellings approved nationally.
 *                    This is the ABS standard for reporting annual totals and is
 *                    more stable than a short-window annualised rate — seasonal
 *                    outliers (e.g. low January figures) are absorbed across 12
 *                    data points rather than amplified.
 *
 * Supply gap       = National Housing Accord target (240,000/yr) minus annual run rate.
 *                    The Accord (September 2022) committed the Commonwealth, states,
 *                    territories and local government to 1.2 million new homes by 2029.
 *
 * % of target      = annual run rate ÷ 240,000 × 100.
 *
 * YoY change       = latest month's approvals compared to the same calendar month
 *                    in the prior year, expressed as a percentage.
 *
 * ── Coverage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Total dwellings = separate houses + other residential (semi-detached, row/terrace,
 * townhouses, flats, apartments). All sectors (private + public).
 * Australia total only — state breakdown in lib/data/state-analysis.ts.
 */

